.TH "CTCSS" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
ctcss \- measure CTCSS tones in multicast PCM audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctcss
.RI "[options] [-I destination ...] [destination ...]"
.SH STATUS
.B Not actively maintained
.SH DESCRIPTION
ctcss receives PCM audio sessions, filters the subaudible band, and reports
the strongest candidate CTCSS/PL tone with its measured level. Output
identifies the RTP SSRC. It is a diagnostic receiver; it does not configure
radiod tone squelch. The source also contains experimental DTMF detection
code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-I destination, \-\-pcm\-in destination"
Add a PCM input group. Repeat for multiple groups; positional groups are also
accepted. At least one input is required.
.TP
.B "\-A interface, \-\-iface interface"
Set default multicast interface.
.TP
.B "\-T hops, \-\-ttl hops"
Set the multicast TTL variable. This receive-only utility does not normally
transmit packets.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics.
.TP
.B "\-V, \-\-Version"
Print version and exit. The capital V in the long option is significant.
.SH INPUT
The current sample loop interprets payload samples as signed 16-bit big-endian
mono PCM and obtains sample rate from the RTP payload mapping. Configure
compatible radiod output; do not feed Opus or float PCM. Preserve subaudible
audio through the receiver filters and demodulator.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect a compatible receiver audio group:
.PP
.nf
ctcss \-I repeater\-pcm.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), monitor(1), pcmrecord(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
